WEBVTT

00:00:00.980 --> 00:00:07.480
Previously on 
The Reflection

00:00:03.810 --> 00:00:07.280
I'm here at Times Square, where the 
memorial ceremony was being held,

00:00:07.280 --> 00:00:09.790
when a terrorist holding what 
appeared to be a flamethrower—

00:00:10.170 --> 00:00:13.890
Now is the time to remind the 
world of our existence!

00:00:21.730 --> 00:00:22.660
There they are.

00:00:23.630 --> 00:00:24.670
I-Guy!

00:00:26.500 --> 00:00:28.630
Our leader's plan

00:00:28.630 --> 00:00:32.490
has finally taken a great step forward.

00:00:32.990 --> 00:00:34.130
Wraith.

00:00:35.470 --> 00:00:36.610
Wraith...

00:00:42.570 --> 00:00:44.980
I have nowhere to go.

00:00:46.010 --> 00:00:47.730
Do you have a car?

00:00:51.970 --> 00:00:54.860
Someday, I want to push on toward the future.

00:00:55.360 --> 00:00:56.870
Like Soar Man?

00:00:58.150 --> 00:00:59.820
Like you.

00:01:08.620 --> 00:01:09.710
Soar Man?

00:01:12.110 --> 00:01:14.260
I got to fly.

00:01:16.410 --> 00:01:17.320
Dad!

00:01:17.770 --> 00:01:18.790
Lisa...

00:03:06.410 --> 00:03:07.610
What is this?

00:03:09.820 --> 00:03:11.440
This situation?

00:03:13.860 --> 00:03:16.320
My laptop's battery is really low.

00:03:19.460 --> 00:03:21.040
She looks like a little kid.

00:03:21.040 --> 00:03:23.020
Well, there are two kids here.

00:03:23.490 --> 00:03:25.390
Yeah, I know.

00:03:25.610 --> 00:03:27.630
I am a kid, after all.

00:03:28.050 --> 00:03:29.720
But Lisa...

00:03:30.180 --> 00:03:32.160
You saw her power, didn't you?

00:03:32.600 --> 00:03:34.400
Power, huh?

00:03:39.180 --> 00:03:41.400
Lisa, this is amazing!

00:03:41.970 --> 00:03:43.700
I somehow got dragged into this.

00:03:47.620 --> 00:03:48.760
And here we go.

00:03:48.760 --> 00:03:49.480
Huh?

00:04:10.160 --> 00:04:11.120
Lisa!

00:04:12.670 --> 00:04:13.590
Lisa!

00:04:32.270 --> 00:04:36.450
And because of that, we almost died...

00:04:37.840 --> 00:04:39.490
And she's still asleep.

00:04:39.950 --> 00:04:42.110
She must have used up all her stamina.

00:04:42.110 --> 00:04:43.610
I'm the same way.

00:04:43.610 --> 00:04:45.920
If I use my powers too much, I feel drained.

00:04:45.920 --> 00:04:47.870
Ack! Wait, wait, wait!

00:04:47.870 --> 00:04:49.510
I made it in time...

00:04:50.470 --> 00:04:53.260
Jennifer Allen, who went missing in New York,

00:04:53.260 --> 00:04:54.820
and May Allen from Dayton.

00:04:55.320 --> 00:04:57.680
I was researching both of them.

00:04:58.260 --> 00:05:00.520
They share a number of similarities.

00:05:01.040 --> 00:05:03.660
First, they're cousins, so they're related.

00:05:04.070 --> 00:05:05.610
They're both women.

00:05:05.610 --> 00:05:08.650
Then I thought, if we need a 
reason for their kidnapping,

00:05:08.650 --> 00:05:11.900
they might also be Reflected.

00:05:12.250 --> 00:05:15.320
So I hacked into the national database

00:05:15.320 --> 00:05:18.770
and looked up areas where the 
Reflection affected many people.

00:05:18.770 --> 00:05:21.300
I cross-referenced hospital records

00:05:21.300 --> 00:05:24.120
with females, members of the 
Allen family, and those who went

00:05:24.120 --> 00:05:25.890
to the hospital after the Reflection.

00:05:25.890 --> 00:05:26.790
And?

00:05:27.700 --> 00:05:29.870
I was able to gather some information.

00:05:30.240 --> 00:05:31.920
It appears that, as they travel,

00:05:31.920 --> 00:05:35.430
they're collecting women 
from the Allen family.

00:05:35.920 --> 00:05:40.240
But given their attack on Lisa, 
it doesn't seem limited to the Allens.

00:05:40.240 --> 00:05:43.590
They're also collecting those 
who may be Reflected.

00:05:43.590 --> 00:05:45.180
And if we narrow it down to Allens?

00:05:45.180 --> 00:05:45.820
Oh...

00:05:46.190 --> 00:05:48.110
Of the closest places,

00:05:48.110 --> 00:05:53.080
someone with the last name "Allen" 
has already gone missing in St. Louis.

00:05:53.410 --> 00:05:57.370
There's also another Allen in the 
next closest city, Kansas City.

00:05:57.830 --> 00:05:59.070
And here.

00:05:59.730 --> 00:06:03.830
Let's throw out Kansas. I'm sure Wraith 
and the rest are already on the move.

00:06:04.370 --> 00:06:07.590
Meaning we should use this chance 
to find the next Allen.

00:06:07.990 --> 00:06:09.570
If we get a hold of her...

00:06:09.570 --> 00:06:11.150
...it'll lead us to Wraith!

00:06:11.570 --> 00:06:13.820
Michelle Allen, age 32.

00:06:13.820 --> 00:06:17.960
She's less closely related than the other 
two, but she's from the same family

00:06:17.960 --> 00:06:19.310
and lives in New Orleans.

00:06:19.310 --> 00:06:20.600
New Orleans?

00:06:21.360 --> 00:06:23.120
New Orleans...

00:06:24.340 --> 00:06:25.330
Jazz!

00:07:05.350 --> 00:07:08.430
<i>Looks like you're completely 
used to that suit now.</i>

00:07:08.430 --> 00:07:11.540
Yeah. But sadly, there haven't 
been any incidents.

00:07:11.540 --> 00:07:13.300
<i>And that's a good thing.</i>

00:07:13.300 --> 00:07:15.920
<i>It means LA is safe again today.</i>

00:07:15.920 --> 00:07:19.680
Like hell it is. No matter 
how used to the suit I get,

00:07:19.680 --> 00:07:22.290
it's pointless if there's 
no stage for me to be on.

00:07:23.210 --> 00:07:25.320
<i>Think about this positively.</i>

00:07:25.670 --> 00:07:31.200
<i>Your very existence might have 
become some kind of deterrent.</i>

00:07:31.200 --> 00:07:32.880
I didn't ask for that.

00:07:34.130 --> 00:07:37.010
I mean, there's no point to 
I-Guy if he doesn't fight.

00:07:37.340 --> 00:07:41.190
A hero is meaningless without villains.

00:07:43.190 --> 00:07:45.140
Hey, are you listening?

00:07:45.490 --> 00:07:49.570
<i>Hey, Ian. There's a gang gathering 
at an abandoned factory.</i>

00:07:49.570 --> 00:07:51.700
A gang at an abandoned factory, eh?

00:07:51.700 --> 00:07:54.220
If that's not fishy, I don't know what is.

00:08:09.520 --> 00:08:12.860
And you're sure we can have these for free?

00:08:12.860 --> 00:08:16.550
Of course. Just make sure 
that you pull the trigger a lot,

00:08:16.550 --> 00:08:19.640
that your shots are heard, 
and that the streets bleed red.

00:08:17.530 --> 00:08:20.300
Damn, this is amazing. Is this real?

00:08:20.300 --> 00:08:23.550
I just want to watch as this city dies.

00:08:39.540 --> 00:08:41.150
Now, then... What will you do?

00:08:44.010 --> 00:08:45.940
Really? You wanna go?

00:08:46.480 --> 00:08:50.560
I don't dislike the way that your 
fighting has livened up this city.

00:08:50.990 --> 00:08:53.420
But there isn't enough violence.

00:08:53.970 --> 00:08:56.470
Sorry, I'm going in a more 
artistic direction.

00:08:59.930 --> 00:09:03.140
I'll show you what true violence is.

00:09:03.140 --> 00:09:04.140
This guy...

00:09:05.470 --> 00:09:08.480
Aaron, this guy isn't a normal 
arms dealer. What do I do?

00:09:08.480 --> 00:09:09.940
<i>Hold him close.</i>

00:09:09.940 --> 00:09:10.810
Huh?

00:09:10.810 --> 00:09:14.150
<i>Hold him close with your song, 
with a soul deeper than the sea.</i>

00:09:14.150 --> 00:09:15.150
I see.

00:09:20.480 --> 00:09:21.330
What?

00:09:27.530 --> 00:09:29.380
The projector's on standby!

00:09:29.380 --> 00:09:30.630
Explosions...

00:09:30.630 --> 00:09:31.830
...are art!

00:09:40.320 --> 00:09:41.840
It's about time for the finale.

00:10:17.040 --> 00:10:19.140
I-Guy, I-Guy, I-Guy...

00:10:19.140 --> 00:10:22.500
His true identity is me, 
the mega-star Ian Izette, damn it.

00:10:23.780 --> 00:10:26.340
Hey, we're holding a press conference! 
Get things set up!

00:10:26.810 --> 00:10:28.250
Hold on.

00:10:29.070 --> 00:10:33.860
Some of the press is bashing you for being 
too soft because villains you apprehended

00:10:33.860 --> 00:10:36.180
have had to be recaptured.

00:10:36.490 --> 00:10:39.300
They're saying the timing was bad.

00:10:39.580 --> 00:10:43.860
"The arms dealer escaped three hours after
capture, with aid from an unknown source."

00:10:43.860 --> 00:10:47.700
"This is the fourth one in a row. All of 
I-Guy's arrests have been pointless."

00:10:47.700 --> 00:10:50.090
"The irresponsible hero, I-Guy."

00:10:50.090 --> 00:10:51.370
And over here...

00:10:51.370 --> 00:10:55.880
"Four girls who look just like magical 
girls from anime appear in Japan."

00:10:55.880 --> 00:10:56.870
Oh, really?

00:10:57.180 --> 00:10:59.310
What happens after the arrest isn't my fault.

00:10:59.310 --> 00:11:00.810
Like that's any of my business!

00:11:00.810 --> 00:11:02.500
Now, calm down, Ian.

00:11:02.500 --> 00:11:05.370
Just announce it when the time is right.

00:11:05.370 --> 00:11:10.150
The issue is who's the real 
star? I-Guy or Ian Izette?

00:11:10.150 --> 00:11:10.960
I-Guy?

00:11:10.960 --> 00:11:14.690
Like hell I'll let the great Ian Izette lose 
to someone who came out of nowhere!

00:11:14.690 --> 00:11:16.890
I'll show them what a true veteran can do!

00:11:17.140 --> 00:11:19.140
Come on now, Ian.

00:11:19.460 --> 00:11:22.160
Jay! Call Trevor, the producer.

00:11:22.520 --> 00:11:24.180
S-Sure...

00:11:26.630 --> 00:11:29.160
<i>Hey, Ian! It's been a while!</i>

00:11:29.160 --> 00:11:30.690
<i>I think it's been about ten years.</i>

00:11:30.690 --> 00:11:33.640
Let's skip the introductions and 
get straight to business.

00:11:33.640 --> 00:11:36.370
You and I are going to make 
a second "Sky Show."

00:11:36.370 --> 00:11:38.690
<i>Yeah! Speaking of "Sky Show"...</i>

00:11:38.690 --> 00:11:42.350
<i>I hear some hero blasting our 
song through LA's blue skies</i>

00:11:42.350 --> 00:11:46.080
<i>as he defeats bad guys is all the rage now!</i>

00:11:46.080 --> 00:11:48.480
<i>What's his name? Nice Guy?</i>

00:11:48.480 --> 00:11:49.500
It's I-Guy.

00:11:49.500 --> 00:11:53.760
<i>Ian, you know him, right? 
Hook me up with him.</i>

00:11:53.760 --> 00:11:56.940
<i>I'll produce an amazing song, 
even greater than "Sky Show"!</i>

00:11:56.940 --> 00:11:58.990
<i>You're working with I-Guy? 
That's amazing, Dad!</i>

00:11:58.990 --> 00:12:01.410
<i>You'll sell at least ten million worldwide.</i>

00:12:01.410 --> 00:12:02.970
<i>Oh, Nice Guy!</i>

00:12:02.970 --> 00:12:03.700
It's I-Guy.

00:12:04.830 --> 00:12:07.780
All everyone talks about 
is I-Guy this, I-Guy that.

00:12:08.400 --> 00:12:10.250
Just you wait, I-Guy!

00:12:10.840 --> 00:12:14.420
I'll show you just how amazing Ian Izette is!

00:12:20.100 --> 00:12:23.630
Hey, if it isn't Ian Izette! 
This takes me back!

00:12:23.630 --> 00:12:26.110
I've been a huge fan for years!

00:12:26.110 --> 00:12:28.760
Everyone will be so happy to see you!

00:12:28.760 --> 00:12:32.940
Go on in. Everyone would be 
ecstatic if you sang a song.

00:12:47.730 --> 00:12:48.450
"Sky Show."

00:12:48.720 --> 00:12:49.660
Huh?

00:12:49.660 --> 00:12:51.580
You know it, right? "Sky Show."

00:12:52.810 --> 00:12:56.460
The huge hit from the 
glorious 80s, "Sky Show."

00:12:58.190 --> 00:12:59.800
Yeah!

00:13:26.080 --> 00:13:29.150
I told you about singing...

00:13:44.300 --> 00:13:47.830
Sorry about that. Looks like he 
had a little too much to drink.

00:13:52.190 --> 00:13:56.230
What's with you? What will come 
of being jealous of yourself?

00:13:56.850 --> 00:13:58.920
Trevor's right.

00:13:58.920 --> 00:14:03.020
What the world wants 
right now isn't Ian Izette.

00:14:03.020 --> 00:14:04.810
Hey, what happened?

00:14:05.150 --> 00:14:07.540
I really wanted to hear "Sky Show."

00:14:24.660 --> 00:14:27.070
Whoa! This is amazing!

00:14:27.070 --> 00:14:28.500
I can't believe it!

00:14:33.470 --> 00:14:53.990
I-Guy! I-Guy! I-Guy! I-Guy!

00:14:41.980 --> 00:14:43.970
"Sky Show!"

00:15:08.170 --> 00:15:11.860
It's so smooth, but it also 
seems extremely durable.

00:15:11.860 --> 00:15:15.520
I bet it's really easy to move in, huh? 
Hey, where did you get this suit?

00:15:15.520 --> 00:15:16.880
Did you make it yourself?

00:15:16.880 --> 00:15:19.880
Yeah, of course heroes make 
their own costumes.

00:15:19.880 --> 00:15:21.450
Sewing machines are a necessity.

00:15:21.800 --> 00:15:23.430
And of course this happens.

00:15:24.020 --> 00:15:25.330
Oh, come on.

00:15:25.330 --> 00:15:27.250
I was thinking...

00:15:27.250 --> 00:15:29.700
If they're gathering Reflected,

00:15:29.700 --> 00:15:33.240
we probably need friends 
who can stand against them.

00:15:35.780 --> 00:15:36.930
He shut up.

00:15:37.540 --> 00:15:41.200
One other thing caught my eye 
when I was doing research earlier.

00:15:41.950 --> 00:15:45.290
There was a woman from 
the Allen family who died.

00:15:45.290 --> 00:15:48.830
And when she was found, 
her young child was missing.

00:15:48.830 --> 00:15:50.840
So the kid was kidnapped, too?

00:15:51.180 --> 00:15:55.350
It was a boy. So it doesn't 
fit the rest of the cases.

00:15:55.810 --> 00:15:57.580
And it's not recent, so...

00:15:58.060 --> 00:15:59.420
But it caught my eye.

00:15:59.750 --> 00:16:01.070
When was this?

00:16:01.070 --> 00:16:02.730
About two and a half years ago.

00:16:02.950 --> 00:16:04.710
So it was after the Reflection.

00:16:04.710 --> 00:16:05.520
Yeah.

00:16:07.470 --> 00:16:08.630
The ocean!

00:16:09.780 --> 00:16:11.650
Oh, wait. The ocean's over here!

00:16:12.550 --> 00:16:15.650
Wow... That ocean breeze feels so nice!

00:16:16.030 --> 00:16:17.130
What's over there?

00:16:17.130 --> 00:16:20.070
Oh, nothing special. 
The ocean's on this side.

00:16:21.480 --> 00:16:24.020
The sign says it's a lake.

00:16:24.920 --> 00:16:28.420
New Orleans 
Louisiana

00:16:41.430 --> 00:16:42.930
And this again...

00:16:43.180 --> 00:16:45.600
I'm sure she hasn't fully recovered yet.

00:16:45.600 --> 00:16:46.980
She got too excited.

00:16:47.550 --> 00:16:49.730
I'll be fine by myself.

00:16:53.260 --> 00:16:54.190
What?

00:16:55.210 --> 00:16:56.110
Nothing.

00:17:23.160 --> 00:17:24.260
This must be it.

00:17:26.140 --> 00:17:27.140
Pardon me...

00:17:27.140 --> 00:17:29.800
Sorry. We're not open yet.

00:17:29.800 --> 00:17:31.890
I came to see Michelle.

00:17:31.890 --> 00:17:33.970
Oh... Michelle...

00:17:35.350 --> 00:17:37.900
Did something happen to Michelle?

00:17:39.180 --> 00:17:43.780
I didn't know that she was a Reflected.

00:17:44.110 --> 00:17:45.790
Wait, you don't mean...

00:17:45.790 --> 00:17:47.380
They took her.

00:17:47.970 --> 00:17:49.940
Merchant and Trader.

00:17:50.530 --> 00:17:54.870
It's just what it sounds like.

00:17:54.870 --> 00:17:55.800
You mean...

00:17:56.350 --> 00:17:59.980
Someone that buys a bunch of 
Reflected and trades them.

00:17:59.980 --> 00:18:02.880
Someone mentioned them to me.

00:18:03.260 --> 00:18:05.820
They're literally a merchant and trader.

00:18:06.600 --> 00:18:10.830
But the goods aren't sold. They're scrapped.

00:18:11.360 --> 00:18:12.310
Scrapped?

00:18:12.980 --> 00:18:15.990
Who knows what's happened 
to Michelle by now?

00:18:15.990 --> 00:18:18.930
Honestly... And I'm 
short-staffed to begin with...

00:18:28.630 --> 00:18:29.920
Come on, stand up.

00:18:30.330 --> 00:18:34.590
I hear you're friends with 
that Reflected, Ben.

00:18:34.590 --> 00:18:38.760
You can't complain if you get 
the same treatment they do.

00:18:39.080 --> 00:18:43.760
You should be kidnapped by 
Merchant and Trader, too.

00:18:44.380 --> 00:18:46.260
Merchant and Trader...

00:18:49.860 --> 00:18:50.360
Here.

00:18:54.870 --> 00:18:56.000
Whoa.

00:18:56.000 --> 00:18:57.440
It's a Reflected!

00:18:57.750 --> 00:18:58.390
It's a Ref!

00:18:58.740 --> 00:19:00.610
There's a Ref over here!

00:19:06.740 --> 00:19:08.440
Clear the way.

00:19:08.440 --> 00:19:09.990
Mr. Dallas, there's a Ref.

00:19:14.530 --> 00:19:17.750
Should I lock you up for vagrancy, or...

00:19:28.440 --> 00:19:30.730
Merchant and Trader...

00:19:31.490 --> 00:19:34.730
You always do have your eye 
out for a good bargain.

00:19:34.730 --> 00:19:38.510
You sure are fast. You have 
a real zeal for business.

00:19:39.170 --> 00:19:44.230
I'll assume the responsibility 
of taking this Reflected.

00:19:44.230 --> 00:19:48.230
We don't mind if you let us deal 
with them every once in a while.

00:19:48.230 --> 00:19:50.170
We have the same goal.

00:19:50.860 --> 00:19:54.190
There's no reason to sully 
the hands of the police.

00:19:54.190 --> 00:19:56.830
The Reflected should deal 
with the Reflected.

00:19:57.970 --> 00:20:00.500
Set a thief to catch a thief or whatever, eh?

00:20:01.310 --> 00:20:03.350
Well, then... To a world without Refs.

00:20:34.720 --> 00:20:38.450
You saw it too, right? That was the 
monster everyone's talking about.

00:20:38.450 --> 00:20:42.410
But what's going to happen 
to that Ref girl he took?

00:20:42.410 --> 00:20:46.730
You don't know? That giant monster eats 'em.

00:20:46.730 --> 00:20:48.220
Whoa, seriously?

00:20:48.400 --> 00:20:53.470
How could he have a creepy 
thing like that as his partner?

00:20:53.770 --> 00:20:55.260
And his eyes...

00:20:55.260 --> 00:20:58.980
Apparently, that monster got to them, too.

00:20:58.980 --> 00:21:01.450
Man, that's scary.

00:21:01.450 --> 00:21:06.980
But it's thanks to them that we 
can drink in peace like this.

00:21:06.980 --> 00:21:09.980
Thanks to Merchant and Trader.

00:21:13.770 --> 00:21:15.290
Then Eleanor was...

00:21:15.620 --> 00:21:19.510
No, it can't be. I'm sure Eleanor is fine...

00:21:19.780 --> 00:21:20.500
Yeah.

00:21:21.160 --> 00:21:22.720
Did that really happen?

00:21:23.510 --> 00:21:25.450
Michelle Allen might have also...

00:21:25.450 --> 00:21:28.430
Huh? Aren't you worried about Eleanor?

00:21:28.430 --> 00:21:29.250
Never mind!

00:21:39.490 --> 00:21:41.730
I'll go look for Eleanor!

00:21:42.010 --> 00:21:43.400
Shut the door for me!

00:22:08.840 --> 00:22:13.060
Yeah, I definitely saw them 
head into the wetlands.

00:22:13.060 --> 00:22:14.550
Just like the intel said.

00:22:14.990 --> 00:22:18.760
I searched the area for a while, but no luck.

00:24:45.000 --> 00:24:55.010
Next Time 
V and Michael

00:24:48.000 --> 00:24:55.010
Narration: Stan Lee
